  <!-- EN: [PAWN_nameDef] was blamed for every broken tool, missing coin, or spoiled crop in the village, often regardless of [PAWN_possessive] involvement. The constant accusations taught [PAWN_pronoun] how to endure hardship and avoid confrontations. [PAWN_pronoun] grew to be resourceful but deeply mistrustful of authority. -->
  <VFEM_VillageScapegoat129.description>[PAWN_nameDef]经常被指责为村庄里所有坏事的罪魁祸首，无论[PAWN_pronoun]是否真的涉及其中。不断的指控让[PAWN_pronoun]学会了承受苦难并避免冲突。[PAWN_pronoun]因此变得足智多谋，但对权威极度不信任。</VFEM_VillageScapegoat129.description>
